# Secrets Management Patterns

## Overview

The platform implements a comprehensive secrets management system that allows users to securely store API keys, tokens, and other sensitive credentials. This system enables bots to authenticate with external services using user-provided credentials.

## Entity Architecture

### Secret Entity
```typescript
@Entity('secrets')
export class Secret {
  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn('uuid')
  id!: string;

  @Column()
  name!: string; // Human-readable name

  @Column({ nullable: true })
  description?: string;

  @Column()
  key!: string; // Environment variable style key (e.g., OPENAI_API_KEY)

  @Column({ type: 'text' })
  encryptedValue!: string; // AES encrypted value

  @Column({ default: 'api_key' })
  type!: 'api_key' | 'oauth_token' | 'bearer_token' | 'basic_auth' | 'custom';

  @Column({ nullable: true })
  provider?: string; // e.g., 'openai', 'github', 'slack'

  @Column({ default: true })
  isActive!: boolean;

  @ManyToOne(() => User, { onDelete: 'CASCADE' })
  user!: Relation<User>;

  @Column()
  userId!: string;

  // Encryption methods
  static encrypt(value: string): string;
  static decrypt(encryptedValue: string): string;
  getDecryptedValue(): string;
  setEncryptedValue(value: string): void;
}
```

## Service Layer

### SecretService
- **Security First**: Never returns decrypted values in API responses
- **Internal Access**: Provides methods for services to access decrypted values
- **User Isolation**: All operations are scoped to the authenticated user
- **Encryption**: Handles all encryption/decryption transparently

```typescript
export class SecretService {
  // Public API methods (never return decrypted values)
  async findAll(userId: string): Promise<SecretSummary[]>;
  async findById(id: string, userId: string): Promise<SecretSummary | null>;
  async create(dto: CreateSecretDto, userId: string): Promise<SecretSummary>;
  async update(id: string, dto: UpdateSecretDto, userId: string): Promise<SecretSummary>;
  async delete(id: string, userId: string): Promise<void>;

  // Internal service methods (return decrypted values)
  async getSecretValueByName(name: string, userId: string): Promise<string | null>;
  async getSecretValueByKey(key: string, userId: string): Promise<string | null>;
}
```

### SecretSummary Interface
```typescript
export interface SecretSummary {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  description?: string;
  key: string;
  type: string;
  provider?: string;
  isActive: boolean;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
  hasValue: boolean; // Indicates if encrypted value exists
}
```

## Encryption Standards

### Environment Variables
```bash
# Required for production
ENCRYPTION_KEY=your-32-character-encryption-key-here
ENCRYPTION_IV=your-16-character-iv-here
```

### Encryption Implementation
- **Algorithm**: AES-256-CBC
- **Key Management**: Environment variables (consider HSM for production)
- **IV**: Fixed for development, should be per-secret for production
- **Error Handling**: Graceful degradation when decryption fails

## API Routes

### Authentication Required
All secrets routes require JWT authentication and operate only on the authenticated user's secrets.

### Route Structure
```typescript
GET    /api/secrets           // List user's secrets (no values)
GET    /api/secrets/:id       // Get specific secret (no value)
POST   /api/secrets           // Create new secret
PUT    /api/secrets/:id       // Update secret
DELETE /api/secrets/:id       // Delete secret
POST   /api/secrets/:id/test  // Test decryption health
```

### Security Headers
- Always validate user ownership
- Never log secret values
- Use proper error messages (don't leak existence)

